    "created_at": "2016-06-22T19:50:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-22T19:50:24Z",
    "body": "@bzbarsky, can you confirm for me that we do not need to do the \"prepare to run a callback\" stuff (which manages the incumbent mechanisms) unless we are saving a callback and calling it later?\n\nE.g. when structured cloning we do a few GetOwnProperty()s. Do we need to manage the backup incumbent settings object stack and increment the skip-when-determining-incumbent counter in those cases? I think that since we are immediately invoking code, those mechanisms are not relevant. But I'd appreciate confirmation.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
